From cb9cd77f5c86d74bd3d5328c2701c510e77c1b00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude [team]" <claude-team@localhost>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:56:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] common/speculative: place each MTP process ubatch once for
 all heads (slot replay)

process() of the draft-mtp driver re-decoded every target batch once per
NextN head after llama_memory_seq_rm(first position). The heads are layers of
one MTP context and share its KV cells, and each head writes only its own
layer. When the first head's batch wrapped around the end of a sliding-window
ring, seq_rm moved the cache head to the lowest freed cell and the later heads
got other cells; the first head's layer then held K/V of other positions under
the cells the later heads named. A batch of several ubatches had a second
failure: the first head's later ubatches took cells that the first ubatch's
window still needed before the later heads ran that ubatch.

llama_memory_set_slot_replay(mem, true) makes llama_kv_cache::prepare() re-use
the cells of the last batch placed without replay when they are all free and
the ubatch shapes match (else it searches as before and warns). process() now
runs each chunk of n_ubatch tokens through every head before the next chunk,
heads 1..H-1 with slot replay, so every head layer holds the K/V of every
position under the cell that holds the position.
LLAMA_SPEC_MTP_NO_SLOT_REPLAY=1 restores the previous order (for A/B runs).

Base: ggml-org/llama.cpp 79e2e74eb11022c1ba2e438df7f0ca2d4c10f8b6.
N21, docs/evidence/2026-10-11-n21-mimo-mtp-heads-fix.md (repo 408032gb).
